Interpretation 1 (distinct sisters): 2.  
Tina's siblings are her brother and her sister; the siblings' sisters are Tina and Tina's sister — two different people.

If you mean per sibling: the brother has 2 sisters (Tina and the sister); the sister has 1 sister (Tina).

(If you summed the numbers per sibling you get 3 sister-relationships: 2 + 1 = 3.)
